...These are some of the problems that I had and what I did about
them...

Listed are a few things to watch out for because they are easy to over
look...


1)  You definately NEED to use the cpp that comes packages with nethack
(DECUS I think).

----> make sure to include the changes to the Makefiles then.


2)  In the included CPP package, comment out this line:
      CPPDEFINE = -DLINE_PREFIX=\"\"


3)  Make sure that SYSTEM is set to Sysatt in the src/Makefile.


4)  When making the src directory, the system may stop at the file
sp_lev.c  Here is what comes up:

   Assembler: tradstdc.h
   aline 2511     :  branch offset is too remote
   *** Error code 1
   Stop

-----> compile this by hand, and use a -g instead of the -O flag that I
used...line will look like this:
   cc -g -I../include -B/usr/tmp/cpp/ -tp -c sp_lev.c
For some reason, this helps (I think because the debuger code catches
it...)


5)  From the top directory, I type in:
    make spec_levs   and 
    make dungeon     and I got the response "Couldn't load shell" and it
exited...  I did have shell defined in the util directory Makefile...

----> The problem was that you have to have SHELL = /bin/sh 
in the top directories Makefile.


6) You have to define the MAKE in the top Makefile also, i.e.:
    MAKE = make
(just uncommment it...)


7) When making from the top directroy, you may get this...:
    Make: Cannot load test.
    *** Error code 1
    Stop

----> Edit the Makefile and comment out the 4 lines of test for both
dungeon AND spec_levs.


8)  When making dgn_comp and sp_comp, after the line:
      mv lex.yy.c dgn_lex.c   (or the appropriate)
I got this:
   ***Error code 2 (ignored)




That is all the problems that I had compiling...sorry it took so long to
get them out, but I had to sit down and recompile...8*(

If you have any other problems, let me know...I may have spotted
something that may help out....

